Package: nanowasm
Title: Run 'WebAssembly' Modules with a Bundled Interpreter
Version: 0.0.0.9001
Authors@R: 
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Loads 'WebAssembly' modules from raw vectors or files and calls
    their exported functions from R. Modules run in a bundled interpreter, so
    no system 'WebAssembly' runtime is needed. R vectors can be copied into
    and out of a module's linear memory, and R functions can be supplied as
    imports. Modules are sandboxed: they have no access to files, network or
    environment beyond the imports they are given, and traps, stack
    exhaustion, memory growth and timeouts are reported as classed R
    conditions.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://pedrobtz.github.io/nanowasm/, https://github.com/pedrobtz/nanowasm
BugReports: https://github.com/pedrobtz/nanowasm/issues
Depends: 
    R (>= 4.3)
Suggests: 
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
